  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Severe periodic frametime spikes causing low average FPS regardless of world complexity, avatar quality, graphics settings, OS, hardware, or VR runtime. Hardware utilisation remains low during spikes, indicating engine-level stalls rather than render bottlenecks. Performance is identical between desktop and vr modes\n\n1% lows are generally rather poor with up to a full second per frame in several worlds\n\nChanging Worlds and Avatars doesnt seem to make much of a difference on linux can see minor gains on windows between worlds and avatars\n\nSpecs \n\nCPU: Ryzen 5 7600\n\nRAM: 32gb DDR5 6000mt/s\n\nGPU: RTX 4070 Super 12gb\n\nStable and Unity 6 Beta on both Windows 11 and Ubuntu 26.04\n\nPerformance 30 - 40 FPS 32 Average\n\nGPU Average Utility 76%\n\nCPU Average Utility per core 65%\n\nRAM 4.6/32\n\nVRAM Average Utility 6.6/11.9\n\nWorlds used for testing\n\nVera's Empty Plane\n\nwrld_7446df4b-d89e-4945-b7a9-4247ff8495a1\n\nA Game About Crates\n\nwrld_9907d48d-47e6-4139-b859-297396ed0f13\n\nFISH !\n\nwrld_ae001ea3-ed05-42f0-adf2-3d47efd10a77\n\n1's Optimized Box\n\nwrld_1a8b8684-3b19-4770-a4a7-288762f57b29",
